# Vanilla Extract

All CSS is `*.css.ts`. Import `style` / `globalStyle` from `@vanilla-extract/css`.

```ts
import { style } from '@vanilla-extract/css';
import { vars } from '@styles/theme.css';
import { Content } from '@styles/layout.css';

export const CustomContent = style([
  Content,
  {
    gap: '.5rem',
    '@media': {
      'screen and (min-width: 30rem)': { fontSize: '1.25rem' },
    },
  },
]);
```

- Colors, borders, text: `vars` from `@styles/theme.css` (not raw hex unless matching an existing exception like badge brand colors).
- Reuse `@styles/layout.css` (`Content`, `List`, `ListItem`, …) and `@styles/typography.css` (`Title`).
- Compose with `style([base, { … }])`. Export PascalCase class names (`Container`, `ListItem`).
- Mobile-first media in rem (`30rem`, `48rem`). JS breakpoint is `MOBILE_BREAKPOINT` (768) — keep CSS and JS in sync when changing it.
- Apply classes via `className={Container}`, never string CSS or inline styles except dynamic values (progress width, header height).
